n incredibly scary thought but it  certainly hasn't stopped the developers  from building here  people should not build houses  here  this tiny strip it's an amazingly small  in a few hundred yards from the river to  here it's a ridiculous place to build  houses it's very worrying because i'm  just down there i'm only about five  minutes walk from the beach  so yes  um i can't imagine that happening look  at all the building that's going on  along the coast here already well it's  scary in it i mean because where i live  in lansing i mean we're quite flat so it  comes over the beach it's going to go up  right up to the main road  i mean the main road floods now is bad  enough and there's putting new estates  up there  and finally you might have noticed it's  getting a little warm out there the met  office is expected to confirm today as  the hottest day of the year so far with  the mercury set to eclipse the record of  27 and a half degrees set in mid-may  they say it marks the start of a heat  wave with temperatures in parts of the  southeast possibly soaring to 34 degrees  on friday the uk reached 34 degrees in  june three times in the past six years  but before that the last time was in  1976.  that is all from us for now thanks so  much for watching
 

